00:21:54.000 --> 00:22:41.000
But the Watcher never made an appearance The broadest family moved in with Maria's parents and their grand house sat empty In February 2015, six months after they had purchased the property The broadesses put 657 boulevard back on the market They asked for nearly $1.5 million, $100,000 more than they had purchased it for With the home's extensive renovations, the skyrocketing real estate market And location in one of New Jersey's premier neighborhoods, it should have been a quick sell However, the Watcher had come to the attention of the local media
但守望者从未露面。布罗杜斯一家搬到了玛丽亚的父母家，他们的大房子空着。2015年2月，即他们购买该房产六个月后，布罗杜斯一家将布勒瓦德657号重新挂牌出售。他们要价近150万美元，比他们买下它的价格高出10万美元。凭借房子的广泛翻修、飙升的房地产市场以及位于新泽西州首要社区之一的位置，这本应该是一次快速的出售。然而，守望者已经引起了当地媒体的注意。

28
00:22:41.000 --> 00:23:18.000
And there were no interested buyers In June 2015, the broadesses filed a lawsuit against the previous owners of 657 John and Andrea Woods According to the morning call, they argued that they never would have bought the property Had they known there was a person who had a quote Mentally disturbed fixation on the house The broadesses were suing for fraud and concealment They believed that the woods should have disclosed the property
并且没有感兴趣的买家。2015年6月，布罗杜斯一家对657号的前业主约翰和安德烈亚·伍兹提起诉讼。据《晨报》（The Morning Call）报道，他们辩称，如果他们知道有一个人对这栋房子有引述“精神错乱的执念”，他们绝不会买下这房产。布罗杜斯一家起诉欺诈和隐瞒。他们认为伍兹应该披露该房产。

